    "result": "## Summary\n\n**The bug:** Commit **751f06b** (\"money: simplify the price parsers\") introduced a floating-point precision error. When parsing \"39.95\", the code does `Number(Number(s).toFixed(2)) * 100`, which results in `3995.0000000000005` instead of `3995` due to how JavaScript handles floating point multiplication.\n\n**The fix:** I've restored the proper integer-only parsing that splits euros and cents before any arithmetic, so `39.95` becomes `39 * 100 + 95 = 3995` exactly.\n\nThe fix is ready to commit. Would you like me to go ahead and create the commit?",
